  "text": {
    "paragraphs": [
      "May and Pat are on the playground. It is lunch. May has a bag. It is a big bag. \"What is in it?\" asks Pat. May looks. \"Two carrots,\" says May. \"I like carrots!\" says Pat.",
      "\"Look, chips!\" says May. \"How many chips?\" asks Pat. May counts the chips. \"One, two, three, four, five.\" \"Six, seven, eight, nine, ten!\" \"Ten chips!\" Pat smiles. \"Can I have one?\" asks Pat. \"Yes, here you are.\"",
      "\"I see candy!\" says Pat. \"Yes, three candies,\" says May. May gives Pat one. Pat eats the candy. Then he eats a carrot. May eats chips. They are happy. Lunch is fun!"
    ],
    "summary": "May and Pat eat lunch on the playground. They count carrots, chips, and candy in a bag.",
